"{\"reasoning\":\"Given the 100\u202f\u00b5W power budget, the tail current Itail must be \u226415\u202f\u00b5A (P=3.3\u202fV\u00b72\u00b7Itail). This yields a maximum transconductance gm1\u22482\u00b7Id/Vov\u22482\u00b77.5\u202f\u00b5A/0.2\u202fV\u224875\u202f\u00b5S (assuming a realistic over\u2011drive Vov\u22480.2\u202fV). The resulting GBW=gm1/(2\u03c0CL)\u224875\u202f\u00b5S/(2\u03c0\u00b75\u202fpF)\u22482.4\u202fMHz, far below the 100\u202fMHz requirement. To reach 100\u202fMHz, gm1\u22483.1\u202fmS is needed, which would require Id\u22480.3\u202fmA per input device and a total power >4\u202fmW, exceeding the 100\u202f\u00b5W limit. Therefore the specified GBW, gain, and power constraints cannot be satisfied simultaneously in the GF180MCU 180\u202fnm 3.3\u202fV process with a 5\u2011transistor OTA topology.\"}"